hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"63","One of the sons of Talha bin Ubaidullah narrated: I was with Umar bin Abdul Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him) when Abu Burdah bin Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) came to him, and he narrated ahadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) through his father. So Umar bin Abdul Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him) called for paper and ink and wrote down those ahadith. Among those ahadith was this hadith: Abu Burdah said, my father narrated to me, he said, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Allah's mercy is upon my Ummah; its punishment is in this world (in the form of trials and tribulations). When the Day of Resurrection comes, followers of other religions will be brought, and Allah the Exalted will give every man a (disbelieving) man, and it will be said to him: This one will go into the Fire in your place."
